{
 "note": "an MQTT PKCS#12 key store without keyStorePassword (the JDK loads it with encrypted safes skipped and no integrity check, keys left unrecovered), (SunX509, the default key manager, and the empty password; NewSunX509's are asyncapi_mqtt_pkcs12_no_password_pkix). The server requires a client certificate (as key-choice's does), so a load that picks no key ends in 'Connection lost'; no broker expectation, which the log would show with a binary matcher's `not` that ours drops",
 "steps": [
  {
   "note": "client.p12, no password, SunX509, MQTT 3",
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/asyncapi",
   "body": {
    "spec": {
     "asyncapi": "2.6.0",
     "info": {
      "title": "Ssl",
      "version": "1"
     },
     "channels": {
      "orders": {
       "publish": {
        "message": {
         "payload": {
          "type": "object"
         }
        }
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "brokerConfig": {
     "mqttBrokerUrl": "ssl://localhost:{{port}}",
     "publishOnLoad": false,
     "mqttSecurity": {
      "sslProperties": {
       "com.ibm.ssl.keyStore": "{{files}}/asyncapi/mqtt-ssl/client.p12",
       "com.ibm.ssl.trustStore": "{{files}}/asyncapi/mqtt-ssl/trust.jks",
       "com.ibm.ssl.trustStorePassword": "changeit"
      }
     }
    }
   },
   "maxMillis": 60000
  },
  {
   "note": "client.p12, no password, SunX509, MQTT 5",
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/asyncapi",
